{
  "run_id": "PMC13114876__problem_constrained__pcd_nodecider_PCD_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 is an example of the multi-phase eutectic HEA addressed by the hypothesis.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial alloy has an intact, naturally formed protective oxide scale at multiphase interfaces under static or low-speed conditions.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing sliding speed increases frictional heating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-speed sliding subjects the oxide layer to cyclic mechanical shear and accumulated stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Frictional heating and mechanical shear cause the protective oxide scale to spall or fragment.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxide disruption occurs preferentially at multiphase interfaces in the eutectic HEA.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removal of the oxide protection exposes fresh alloy substrate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Freshly exposed alloy surfaces undergo rapid local corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxide layer can protect the sliding surface and suppress deformation or material loss.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::028::adaptive_friction_interface_protection",
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The exposed surface repassivates after oxide delamination, producing a repeated spallation-repassivation cycle.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Loss and fragmentation of the protective oxide promote spallation, pit formation, and accelerated material loss.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Repeated oxide removal and fresh-metal exposure accelerate corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide-spallation and repassivation cycle synergistically accelerates both wear and corrosion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-speed sliding produces significantly greater total degradation than a static or low-speed baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wear rates are markedly higher at high sliding speed because of rapid oxide spallation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::036::3_2_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localized corrosion depth increases at high sliding speed because fresh material is repeatedly exposed.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under static or low-speed baseline conditions, the oxide layer remains largely intact and synergistic degradation is minimal.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies to multi-phase eutectic HEAs under simultaneous wear and corrosion at approximately 550 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Frictional heating and mechanical stresses are the primary causes of oxide degradation, while other thermal oxidation phenomena are secondary.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
